🎂
"Happy Birthday"/en
=== start/en
¶Happy Birthday in three parts: a melody, a harmony under it, and chords
holding both up.

Every part is written in scale degrees, so 1 is the tonic and 8 is the tonic
an octave up. That's why the tune reads the same whatever key you put it in —
change @Music/key and the whole song moves with it, singers included.

The melody and the harmony move in half beats and the chords in whole ones,
so each part says how long its own entries are and they still line up.¶

¶Beats since the song started, so the cake can move with it. @Beat is ø until
music plays, so it needs a guard.¶
beat: Beat()
count: beat•ø ? 0 beat.count

¶The tune. Two eighths, then longer notes — the rests are what make the
rhythm, since every entry lasts the same half beat.¶
melody: [
	5 5 6 ø 5 ø 8 ø 7 ø ø ø
	5 5 6 ø 5 ø 9 ø 8 ø ø ø
	5 5 12 ø 10 ø 8 ø 7 ø 6 ø
	ø 11 11 10 ø 8 ø 9 ø 8 ø ø
	ø ø ø ø
]

¶A second voice below the melody, in the same half beats.¶
alto: [
	5 5 3 ø 3 ø 3 ø 4 ø ø ø
	4 4 4 ø 4 ø 4 ø 5 ø ø ø
	5 5 5 ø 8 ø 5 ø 5 ø 4 ø
	6 6 6 ø 6 ø 5 ø 5 ø ø ø
	ø ø ø ø
]

¶Chords, one per beat. A set sounds its degrees together, so {1 3 5} is the
tonic triad and {4 5 7 9} is the one that wants to resolve back to it.¶
chords: [
	ø {1 3 5} ø ø {4 5 7 9} ø
	ø ø ø ø {1 3 5} ø
	ø ø ø ø {4 6 8} ø
	ø ø {1 3 5} ø {4 5 7 9} {1 3 5}
	ø ø
]

¶The cake swells on every beat and settles between them.¶
ƒ cake() 💬('🎂' (4m + ((count % 2) · 0.4m)) duration: 0.2s)

🎭(
	[
		🔳(
			Stack(padding: 0.5m)
			[
				cake()
				💬('Happy Birthday' 1.3m)
			]
		)
		🎼(
			[
				🎶(melody instrument: 🔈.🪈 beat: 0.5beats)
				🎶(alto instrument: 🔈.🎻 beat: 0.5beats volume: 65%)
				🎶(chords instrument: 🔈.🎹 beat: 1beats volume: 55%)
			]
			tempo: 116beats/min
			name: 'birthday'
		)
	]
	background: Color(18% 20 330°)
	color: Color(96% 0 0°)
)
